{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>And Daniel prospered in the kingdom of Darius and in the kingdom of Cyrus the Persian</b> — And this indicates that he did not live longer, for he was old. And Sheshbazzar is Zerubbabel, not Daniel, by two proofs: concerning Zerubbabel he said: peḥat Yehudah, and 'Sheshbazzar was his name, for peḥah was his name.' And another proof, greater and stronger than this: Zechariah said: 'The hands of Zerubbabel founded this house,' and so it is written in the book of Ezra, and there it is written: 'Then Sheshbazzar this one came, laid the foundations of the house of Elohim in Jerusalem.'"], :book :daniel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Daniel - Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/daniel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:20:14.836130045Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}